WEBVTT

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:02.911


00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.812
<b>My name is Anita Stelzner,</b>

00:01:10.812 --> 00:01:17.151
<b>I was born on the 26th of September 1942 in Zechin.</b>

00:01:17.735 --> 00:01:23.157
<b>In 1964 I got married for the first time.</b>

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:28.538
<b>And straight away I had</b>
<b>my first daughter,</b>

00:01:28.538 --> 00:01:29.998
<b>Ramona.</b>

00:01:31.207 --> 00:01:35.795
<b>One year and ten months later</b>

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.588
<b>came my second daughter.</b>

00:01:37.839 --> 00:01:42.176
<b>That was the end of it.</b>

00:01:44.595 --> 00:01:47.348
<b>Then we just got by</b>

00:01:47.348 --> 00:01:49.100
<b>still with my husband.</b>

00:01:50.101 --> 00:01:53.521
<b>And I had a good friend,</b>

00:01:54.397 --> 00:01:57.859
<b>she lived just up the road in the village.</b>

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:01.612
<b>And I lived at the back</b>
<b>where I was employed,</b>

00:02:01.612 --> 00:02:06.367
<b>and we went ‘swaying’ together,</b>
<b>that's what we called it, ‘swaying’.</b>

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:08.828
<b>That was the expression in our village.</b>

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:12.290
<b>‘Did you go out swaying today?’or ‘Will you go swaying?’</b>
<b>- ‘Yes’</b>

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:14.584
<b>‘Come on, let's get out of here.’</b>

00:02:14.584 --> 00:02:18.921
<b>Then we tried</b>

00:02:21.549 --> 00:02:23.593
<b>to dance rock'n'roll.</b>

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:27.138
<b>And that didn't work out.</b>

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:30.433
<b>Did you like to waltz?</b>

00:02:30.558 --> 00:02:34.729
<b>What? - Waltz?</b>
<b>Waltz...</b>

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:38.900
<b>I have to tell you, don't I?</b>

00:02:40.068 --> 00:02:45.198
<b>I was 15 years old when I first went to</b>
<b>a dance floor</b>

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:48.159
<b>and I never stopped.</b>

00:02:48.493 --> 00:02:50.870
<b>Every weekend.</b>

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:44.382
<b>There was a time in our lives</b>

00:03:45.007 --> 00:03:48.678
<b>when we danced every day.</b>

00:03:50.555 --> 00:03:52.807
<b>I won't ever forget</b>

00:03:52.807 --> 00:03:55.184
<b>how you held me.</b>

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:06.195
<b>I don't think I ever told you</b>

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:09.365
<b>how happy it made me</b>

00:04:09.365 --> 00:04:13.119
<b>that you were by my side.</b>

00:04:17.665 --> 00:04:21.711
<b>With you, time always flew by.</b>

00:04:55.870 --> 00:05:02.710
<b>Unfortunately, I can't remember</b>
<b>our last dance together.</b>

00:05:07.965 --> 00:05:12.303
<b>But you were always in my thoughts.</b>

00:05:50.925 --> 00:05:57.139
<b>Hello, I'm Adetayo Manuwa.</b>
<b>Most people know me as Tutipsy.</b>

00:05:59.934 --> 00:06:03.145
<b>I am 29 years old</b>
<b>and I come from Nigeria.</b>

00:06:03.145 --> 00:06:08.234
<b>I moved to Dessau in November 2017</b>
<b>to study there.</b>

00:06:09.568 --> 00:06:12.571
<b>Music has given me a great...</b>

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:15.533
<b>Okay, I'll do that in English.</b>

00:06:19.203 --> 00:06:23.416
<b>In 2019, I had the opportunity to be part</b>
<b>of the One Community project</b>

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:26.419
<b>where I worked with senior citizens</b>
<b>and sang with them.</b>

00:06:26.711 --> 00:06:33.301
<b>And the thing about it was that it made me see</b>
<b>how music can break down barriers.</b>

00:06:41.017 --> 00:06:45.855
<b>After the success of the One Community project</b>
<b>came Corona in 2020.</b>

00:06:45.855 --> 00:06:48.274
<b>And that was the biggest shock.</b>

00:06:48.274 --> 00:06:49.358
<b>It affected me also</b>

00:06:49.358 --> 00:06:51.861
<b>when I couldn't get a job</b>
<b>and I was really broke.</b>

00:06:52.069 --> 00:06:55.614
<b>And when I visited the Marienheim,</b>
<b>they asked me: ‘How am I doing?’</b>

00:06:55.614 --> 00:06:58.200
<b>And I was like:</b>
<b>‘I'm not doing fine.’</b>

00:06:58.367 --> 00:07:04.290
<b>They all really wanted me to be happy</b>
<b>and I was offered a job at the Marienheim.</b>

00:07:04.915 --> 00:07:08.419
<b>That was one of the biggest shifts</b>
<b>of my life, I would say.</b>

00:07:08.878 --> 00:07:14.300
<b>It was just a regular day,</b>
<b>I was speaking to one of our residents.</b>

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:17.887
<b>And I told him that</b>
<b>I would like to learn the waltz.</b>

00:07:18.054 --> 00:07:21.015
<b>And there was Mrs. Sturm and she was like:</b>

00:07:21.015 --> 00:07:23.559
<b>'You can't dance a waltz?</b>
<b>- I'll teach you!"</b>

00:07:23.559 --> 00:07:25.019
<b>She had a walker.</b>

00:07:25.019 --> 00:07:30.149
<b>And that was funny, because she stood up</b>
<b>and we started to dance and tried to practise.</b>

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:35.488
<b>And everyone started to talk about</b>
<b>dance lessons, the good times that they had.</b>

00:07:36.655 --> 00:07:39.116
<b>They were talking about</b>
<b>how it was in that time.</b>

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:43.329
<b>And everybody...The room was lifted up.</b>

00:07:43.329 --> 00:07:45.998
<b>And I was like, ‘Okay, what's going on here?’</b>

00:07:45.998 --> 00:07:52.505
<b>I thought about, okay, what about</b>
<b>finding something to bring people together?</b>

00:07:52.505 --> 00:07:56.425
<b>Another form of a project
<b>that we use dance to bring people together.</b></b>

00:08:06.268 --> 00:08:11.148
<b>About me and how I love those old ball nights</b>
<b>which I find really great.</b>

00:08:11.649 --> 00:08:13.192
<b>Yes?</b>

00:08:14.235 --> 00:08:17.947
<b>I am Jolene Rätz, I am 21,</b>
<b>I come from Dessau,</b>

00:08:17.947 --> 00:08:19.990
<b>but I'm studying educational science in Halle</b>

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:24.578
<b>and I am a co-organiser</b>
<b>of the One Community Gala.</b>

00:08:25.037 --> 00:08:27.581
<b>My connection to the waltz</b>

00:08:27.581 --> 00:08:30.418
<b>and dancing has always been through my parents.</b>

00:08:30.418 --> 00:08:32.420
<b>They go dancing every week.</b>

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:34.839
<b>And that's also</b>
<b>my connection to the waltz in general.</b>

00:08:34.839 --> 00:08:36.382
<b>This being together</b>

00:08:36.382 --> 00:08:40.136
<b>and how people through dancing</b>
<b>and through music</b>

00:08:40.136 --> 00:08:43.055
<b>and especially through the waltz</b>
<b>can be brought together.</b>

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:46.225
<b>And I personally</b>
<b>find it so beautiful because</b>

00:08:46.225 --> 00:08:50.354
<b>I'm reminded of ball nights of the past,</b>
<b>how people came together,</b>

00:08:50.354 --> 00:08:51.814
<b>how they had fun together,</b>

00:08:51.939 --> 00:08:55.151
<b>and that's exactly what we wanted to achieve</b>
<b>with the One Community Gala now.</b>

00:08:55.776 --> 00:08:59.447
<b>Of course, it was quite an up and down</b>
<b>because it was also unbelievable, of course.</b>

00:08:59.447 --> 00:09:03.367
<b>A lot of organisation had to be done</b>
<b>and there were always new challenges</b>

00:09:03.367 --> 00:09:06.370
<b>and hurdles that had to be overcome,</b
<b>for which you had to be prepared.</b></b>

00:09:06.829 --> 00:09:09.915
<b>But then above all to see this first rehearsal</b>

00:09:09.915 --> 00:09:12.710
<b>and to see that it works</b>

00:09:13.169 --> 00:09:15.880
<b>that the plan really works</b>
<b>these people come together,</b>

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:18.340
<b>they have fun together,</b>
<b>and they are dancing.</b>

00:09:18.716 --> 00:09:20.509
<b>I can't describe it,</b>

00:09:20.509 --> 00:09:22.094
<b>it is so nice to experience that</b>

00:09:22.094 --> 00:09:23.262
<b>and so nice to see</b>

00:09:23.262 --> 00:09:25.931
<b>and that just triggers so much gratitude in me</b>

00:09:25.931 --> 00:09:27.892
<b>and so much joy to be part of it.</b>

00:09:27.892 --> 00:09:29.477
<b>It is beyond description.</b>

00:09:33.981 --> 00:09:37.109
<b>When I came back from being a prisoner of war</b>

00:09:37.359 --> 00:09:40.654
<b>there were my friends,</b>

00:09:40.654 --> 00:09:42.323
<b>especially the younger ones,</b>

00:09:43.032 --> 00:09:45.993
<b>who were now unable to attend a dance school</b>

00:09:45.993 --> 00:09:49.788
<b>and did not have the opportunity</b>
<b>to learn to dance.</b>

00:09:50.289 --> 00:09:53.209
<b>So we did it at home with them,</b>

00:09:53.209 --> 00:09:56.712
<b>we practised dancing in the living room.</b>

00:09:57.588 --> 00:10:00.174
<b>So my name is Horst Kaczmarek,</b>

00:10:00.174 --> 00:10:03.302
<b>am 95 years old</b>

00:10:03.302 --> 00:10:05.763
<b>and worked as a teacher.</b>

00:10:05.763 --> 00:10:10.601
<b>I was married for 74 years.</b>

00:10:11.101 --> 00:10:13.938
<b>I may already be</b>
<b>quite an old person,</b>

00:10:14.647 --> 00:10:17.149
<b>but before my wife died,</b</b>

00:10:18.067 --> 00:10:21.987
<b>we often danced at home</b>

00:10:21.987 --> 00:10:25.741
<b>by ourselves just for us.</b>

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:29.745
<b>When I think of a waltz?</b>

00:10:29.745 --> 00:10:34.542
<b>Well, my wife always said to me:</b>

00:10:34.542 --> 00:10:37.753
<b>‘Don't shake your shoulders.’</b>

00:10:41.257 --> 00:10:44.593
<b>So with today's young generation</b>

00:10:45.511 --> 00:10:49.557
<b>the waltz has certainly lost its significance.</b>

00:10:50.182 --> 00:10:53.394
<b>As important as it</b>

00:10:53.394 --> 00:11:01.443
<b>was in my parents' day,</b>

00:11:01.443 --> 00:11:03.571
<b>it's not today any more.</b>

00:11:03.737 --> 00:11:10.202
<b>But it's still the dance that</b>

00:11:10.202 --> 00:11:12.162
<b>has a special grandeur.</b>

00:11:59.668 --> 00:12:02.046
<b>My name is Antje Thomas,</b>

00:12:02.046 --> 00:12:04.131
<b>I am 64 years old</b>

00:12:04.131 --> 00:12:08.552
<b>and have been working here at the facility since 1974</b>

00:12:08.802 --> 00:12:11.221
<b>I started as a student nurse,</b>

00:12:11.221 --> 00:12:14.308
<b>and later trained as a nursing service manager.</b>

00:12:14.308 --> 00:12:16.727
<b>Before that, I also</b>
<b>became a physiotherapist</b>

00:12:16.727 --> 00:12:20.314
<b>and since around 2005</b>

00:12:20.314 --> 00:12:23.400
<b>I manage the home of the</b>
<b>Anhaltische Diakonissen Anstalt Dessau.</b>

00:12:23.484 --> 00:12:27.446
<b>Music is something wonderful for the residents.</b>

00:12:27.446 --> 00:12:29.239
<b>They respond to it immediately.</b>

00:12:29.239 --> 00:12:31.784
<b>The music they know touches them.</b>

00:12:31.784 --> 00:12:35.412
<b>I once heard that ones music taste</b>
<b>is fully formed at the age of 30.</b>

00:12:35.412 --> 00:12:40.793
<b>That means we have to use music</b>
<b>from the youth of our residents.</b>

00:12:40.834 --> 00:12:43.837
<b>Now there was, as I said, the waltz as a theme</b>

00:12:43.837 --> 00:12:49.843
<b>and actually in this generation</b>
<b>everyone went to dance school.</b>

00:12:49.885 --> 00:12:53.889
<b>And the waltz is</b>
<b>the most normal thing in the world for them.</b>

00:12:53.889 --> 00:12:55.766
<b>And suddenly they can all do it too.</b>

00:12:55.766 --> 00:12:57.351
<b>Yes, and I'm amazed:</b>

00:12:57.351 --> 00:13:01.105
<b>We have a resident who really</b>
<b>lasted through the whole waltz</b>

00:13:01.105 --> 00:13:02.648
<b>And it was long.</b>

00:13:03.023 --> 00:13:05.859
<b>The young people were very reserved</b>

00:13:05.859 --> 00:13:08.946
<b>and didn't really know what to expect.</b>

00:13:08.946 --> 00:13:12.241
<b>And for the older residents in our facility</b>

00:13:12.241 --> 00:13:13.784
<b>it was rather strange,</b>

00:13:13.784 --> 00:13:16.453
<b>because there were others, strangers to them.</b>

00:13:16.453 --> 00:13:19.832
<b>But it plays a role</b>
<b>that they are so young.</b>

00:13:20.207 --> 00:13:22.626
<b>The old people think that's good</b>

00:13:22.626 --> 00:13:24.420
<b>and they can get involved.</b>

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:28.132
<b>And I noticed that the students</b>
<b>also quickly gained confidence</b>

00:13:28.132 --> 00:13:33.011
<b>and realised, oh, that's all they want from us,</b>
<b>we should dance with them.</b>

00:13:33.011 --> 00:13:35.764
<b>And we were many different nationalities.</b>

00:13:35.764 --> 00:13:38.851
<b>And after we also danced the,</b>

00:13:38.851 --> 00:13:40.310
<b>what's the name of the dance?</b>

00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:42.938
<b>Discofox, when we danced that</b>

00:13:42.938 --> 00:13:48.777
<b>the students simply felt like</b>
<b>performing their own dance as well.</b>

00:13:48.777 --> 00:13:51.238
<b>And that really impressed our residents.</b>

00:13:51.238 --> 00:13:52.948
<b>One resident said:</b>

00:13:52.948 --> 00:13:57.119
<b>"Now I've seen it for real</b>
<b>and not just on television."</b>

00:13:57.119 --> 00:14:03.625
<b>And I also liked the fact that they were</b>
<b>not just prepared to adopt our culture,</b>

00:14:03.625 --> 00:14:07.045
<b>but that we also got to know their culture.</b>

00:14:28.567 --> 00:14:34.364
<b>I had lessons in Arabic dance and belly dance,</b</b>

00:14:34.364 --> 00:14:38.202
<b>but that was in 2015, I think.</b>

00:14:38.202 --> 00:14:38.744
<b>Yes.</b>

00:14:38.952 --> 00:14:41.497
<b>My name is Iryna Braunshtein</b>

00:14:41.497 --> 00:14:43.457
<b>and I am 31 years old.</b>

00:14:43.457 --> 00:14:46.084
<b>And I came here from the Ukraine,</b>

00:14:46.084 --> 00:14:47.503
<b>because of the war.</b>

00:14:47.503 --> 00:14:49.671
<b>I'm studying German here.</b>

00:14:49.671 --> 00:14:52.132
<b>Yes, I'm learning German</b>

00:14:52.132 --> 00:14:54.635
<b>and I want to live here.</b>

00:14:55.302 --> 00:14:59.473
<b>I just enjoyed this time.</b>
<b>I really enjoyed this time.</b>

00:14:59.723 --> 00:15:04.853
<b>And it helps to understand that</b>
<b>you have to respect everyone</b>

00:15:05.187 --> 00:15:08.607
<b>and it's a great opportunity</b>

00:15:08.607 --> 00:15:11.485
<b>to spend time with these people.</b>

00:15:13.195 --> 00:15:16.114
<b>The experience is exciting, really.</b>

00:15:16.615 --> 00:15:25.374
<b>I like dancing and my dance partner Wolfgang</b>

00:15:25.374 --> 00:15:27.167
<b>also likes to dance.</b>

00:15:27.334 --> 00:15:31.880
<b>I think he was and is a great dancer.</b>

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:37.469
<b>And it was just really funny</b>
<b>and very exciting</b>

00:15:37.469 --> 00:15:40.681
<b>And it was fun</b>
<b>to be dancing with this man.</b>

00:15:40.681 --> 00:15:43.475
<b>And yes, it was great.</b>

00:15:44.643 --> 00:15:47.855
<b>This project doesn't just have a huge impact</b>

00:15:47.855 --> 00:15:53.610
<b>on my learning progress of the German language,</b</b>

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:56.989
<b>but also on the atmosphere in our classroom,</b>

00:15:56.989 --> 00:16:04.705
<b>because we go to the old people's home ‘together’</b>

00:16:04.705 --> 00:16:07.291
<b>and we do something together.</b>

00:16:07.291 --> 00:16:09.376
<b>This is really huge.</b>

00:16:42.326 --> 00:16:48.832
<b>We met here in Dessau, basically after the war,</b>
<b>and got to know each other.</b>

00:16:48.832 --> 00:16:51.001
<b>I am 90</b>

00:16:51.001 --> 00:16:52.502
<b>and she is 88.</b>

00:16:52.502 --> 00:16:56.340
<b>We are both Dessau natives, if you like.</b>

00:16:57.341 --> 00:17:00.427
<b>Yes, she was born in Berlin,</b</b>

00:17:00.427 --> 00:17:02.763
<b>but is here in Dessau...</b>

00:17:02.763 --> 00:17:04.973
<b>- I was a flower from Berlin.</b>

00:17:04.973 --> 00:17:07.476
<b>- You were? You still are now.</b>
<b>- I am still now.</b>

00:17:09.519 --> 00:17:12.356
<b>Can you still remember when you</b>
<b>danced together for the first time?</b>

00:17:14.066 --> 00:17:16.818
<b>That was at Anton's, wasn't it?</b>
<b>- At Anton's, yes.</b>

00:17:17.903 --> 00:17:20.697
<b>Yes, then you liked me again,</b>
<b>not before.</b>

00:17:20.697 --> 00:17:22.491
<b>- We couldn't stand each other.</b>

00:17:24.743 --> 00:17:30.040
<b>Yes, the main music back then was the waltz.</b>

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:32.292
<b>That was mostly played.</b>

00:17:32.292 --> 00:17:35.087
<b>The last time we danced was at our</b>

00:17:35.087 --> 00:17:37.631
<b>Diamond wedding, right?</b>

00:17:37.631 --> 00:17:38.966
<b>That was 10 years ago..</b>

00:17:39.299 --> 00:17:42.010
<b>Nobody taught us how to dance, did they?</b>
<b>- No.</b>

00:17:42.636 --> 00:17:46.473
<b>And I'll be honest, we really miss it.</b>

00:17:46.473 --> 00:17:49.893
<b>This is still weighing on us in our old age</b>

00:17:49.893 --> 00:17:54.022
<b>and especially since we've been here,</b>
<b>that weighs on us.</b>

00:17:54.773 --> 00:18:00.320
<b>We now have rooms,</b>
<b>which are right next to each other.</b>

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:02.656
<b>And she has a television in her room</b>

00:18:02.656 --> 00:18:04.157
<b>and I have the radio.</b>

00:18:06.034 --> 00:18:12.332
<b>And I always put a CD</b>
<b>in the radio in the evening,</b</b>

00:18:12.332 --> 00:18:14.960
<b>mainly with waltzes and folk music.</b>

00:18:16.378 --> 00:18:21.717
<b>I let them play</b>
<b>until the disc is finished.</b>

00:18:22.509 --> 00:18:25.804
<b>I'm usually gone before then.</b>

00:18:25.804 --> 00:18:27.055
<b>Asleep.</b>

00:18:27.055 --> 00:18:29.599
<b>The radio switches itself off.</b>

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:36.606
<b>Hello, my name is Ines,</b>
<b>I am 33 years old</b>

00:18:36.606 --> 00:18:41.111
<b>and I work as a product developer</b>
<b>for a start-up company.</b>

00:18:41.236 --> 00:18:45.449
<b>Well, I have the feeling that the waltz</b>
<b>is definitely not extinct.</b>

00:18:45.449 --> 00:18:48.326
<b>It always comes back at certain</b>
<b>points in our lives.</b>

00:18:48.326 --> 00:18:50.287
<b>When I first heard about the project,</b>

00:18:50.287 --> 00:18:53.290
<b>I was simply delighted,</b>
